<p>The Google APIs Explorer is a tool available on most REST API method
documentation pages that lets you try Google API methods without writing co=
de.
The APIs Explorer acts on real data, so use caution when trying methods tha=
t
create, modify, or delete data.</p>

<h2 id=3D"use_the_directory" data-text=3D"Use the directory" tabindex=3D"-1=
" role=3D"presentation"><span class=3D"devsite-heading" role=3D"heading" ar=
ia-level=3D"2">Use the directory</span><button type=3D"button" class=3D"dev=
site-heading-link button-flat material-icons" aria-label=3D"Copy link to th=
is section: Use the directory" data-title=3D"Copy link to this section: Use=
 the directory" data-id=3D"use_the_directory"></button></h2>

<p>For a list of Google APIs you can explore, browse the
<a href=3D"https://developers.google.com/apis-explorer">Google APIs Explore=
r Directory</a>. This list contains links to
the API reference documentation for supported APIs. Follow the steps below =
to
explore the API:</p>

<ol>
<li>Open the <a href=3D"https://developers.google.com/apis-explorer">Google=
 APIs Explorer Directory</a>.</li>
<li>In the search box at the top, enter the name of the API you want to exp=
lore.</li>
<li>Click the name of the API. This opens the API reference documentation.<=
/li>
<li>At the left, click the method you want to use in the navigation.</li>
<li><p>At the right, find the panel labeled "Try this method." See below fo=
r details
about how to use the APIs Explorer side panel and how to expand it into the
full-screen APIs Explorer panel.</p>
<aside class=3D"note"><strong>Note:</strong><span> If you don't see the API=
s Explorer side panel, the method might not be
compatible with APIs Explorer.</span></aside></li>
</ol>

<h2 id=3D"use_the_side_panel" data-text=3D"Use the side panel" tabindex=3D"=
-1" role=3D"presentation"><span class=3D"devsite-heading" role=3D"heading" =
aria-level=3D"2">Use the side panel</span><button type=3D"button" class=3D"=
devsite-heading-link button-flat material-icons" aria-label=3D"Copy link to=
 this section: Use the side panel" data-title=3D"Copy link to this section:=
 Use the side panel" data-id=3D"use_the_side_panel"></button></h2>

<figure class=3D"attempt-right">
  <img src=3D"https://developers.google.com/static/explorer-help/guides/ima=
ges/condensed.png" data-modal-dialog-id=3D"side-panel" alt=3D"APIs Explorer=
 side panel for the Google Books API" class=3D"screenshot devsite-lightbox-=
image" role=3D"button" aria-label=3D"View enlarged image (APIs Explorer sid=
e panel for the Google Books API)" data-title=3D"APIs Explorer side panel f=
or the Google Books API" tabindex=3D"0">
  <figcaption><b>Figure 1</b>: APIs Explorer side panel for the Google Book=
s API.</figcaption>
</figure>

<p><devsite-lightbox id=3D"side-panel"><button class=3D"devsite-dialog-clos=
e devsite-lightbox-icon-close" tabindex=3D"1" aria-label=3D"Close dialog"><=
/button>
  <img src=3D"https://developers.google.com/static/explorer-help/guides/ima=
ges/condensed.png">
</devsite-lightbox></p>

<p>By default, the APIs Explorer appears on the right-hand side of the scre=
en in
API reference documentation for supported methods.</p>

<p>You can customize and interact with the following sections in the APIs E=
xplorer
side panel:</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Request parameters</strong>, if required by the method.</li>
<li><strong>Request body</strong>, if required by the method.</li>
<li><strong>Credentials</strong>, to test the method with various credentia=
l
types and scopes.</li>
<li><strong>Execute</strong> button, to run the method using the parameters=
 and settings
you've specified.</li>
<li><strong>Result</strong>, displayed only after executing the method.</li=
>
</ul>

<h2 id=3D"use_the_full-screen_panel" class=3D"clear" data-text=3D"Use the f=
ull-screen panel" tabindex=3D"-1">Use the full-screen panel</h2>

<figure class=3D"attempt-right">
  <img src=3D"https://developers.google.com/static/explorer-help/guides/ima=
ges/expanded.png" data-modal-dialog-id=3D"fullscreen-panel" alt=3D"APIs Exp=
lorer full-screen panel for the Google Books API" class=3D"screenshot devsi=
te-lightbox-image" role=3D"button" aria-label=3D"View enlarged image (APIs =
Explorer full-screen panel for the Google Books API)" data-title=3D"APIs Ex=
plorer full-screen panel for the Google Books API" tabindex=3D"0">
  <figcaption><b>Figure 2</b>: APIs Explorer full-screen panel for the Goog=
le Books API.</figcaption>
</figure>

<p><devsite-lightbox id=3D"fullscreen-panel"><button class=3D"devsite-dialo=
g-close devsite-lightbox-icon-close" tabindex=3D"1" aria-label=3D"Close dia=
log"></button>
  <img src=3D"https://developers.google.com/static/explorer-help/guides/ima=
ges/expanded.png">
</devsite-lightbox></p>

<p>In the collapsed APIs Explorer side panel, you can click Full screen
<span class=3D"material-icons" aria-hidden=3D"true" translate=3D"no">fullsc=
reen</span> to expand the APIs Explorer. The
full-screen panel displays an extra pane containing code samples,
<code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">application/json</code> responses, and R=
aw HTTP responses.</p>

<h2 id=3D"authentication" class=3D"clear" data-text=3D"Authentication" tabi=
ndex=3D"-1">Authentication</h2>

<p>The APIs Explorer uses its own credentials to make a request. You can't =
use
custom credentials with the APIs Explorer.</p>

<h2 id=3D"data_formats" data-text=3D"Data formats" tabindex=3D"-1">Data for=
mats</h2>

<p>The APIs Explorer only supports JSON for responses and request payloads.=
 Even if
your API supports other data formats, these formats don't work in the
APIs Explorer.</p>

<h2 id=3D"next_steps" data-text=3D"Next steps" tabindex=3D"-1">Next steps</=
h2>

<ul>
<li>Learn how to <a href=3D"https://developers.google.com/explorer-help/exe=
cute-method">display the APIs Explorer and execute a method</a>.</li>
<li>Learn how to <a href=3D"https://developers.google.com/explorer-help/aut=
horization-and-authentication">test a method using different credentials an=
d scopes</a>.</li>
<li>Learn how to <a href=3D"https://developers.google.com/explorer-help/cod=
e-samples">execute APIs Explorer sample code locally</a>.</li>
</ul>

